WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:04.740
Titan is the largest moon of Saturn and the second largest in the Solar System.

00:05.199 --> 00:16.091
It is the only moon that is known to have a dense atmosphere, and is the only known object in the Solar System besides Earth with clear evidence of stable bodies of surface liquid.

00:16.592 --> 00:23.092
Titan is one of seven gravitationally rounded moons of Saturn, and is the second-most distant among them.

00:23.662 --> 00:33.066
Frequently described as a planet-like moon, Titan is 48.16% larger in diameter than Earth's moon, and 80% more massive.
